[?2004hroot@f5f6f676680c:/app# cd /app && cat >> README.md <<'EOF'
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Delta checkpoints and catalog upgrades
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Each page's product changes and cursor are committed in one transaction,
[?2004l[?2004h> including tombstone-only and compacted/empty pages. If a run fails, rerunning
[?2004l[?2004h> `sync` resumes after the last committed page. An unchanged feed requires just
[?2004l[?2004h> one request at the saved cursor to check for new changes.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Existing insert-only catalogs are upgraded automatically: duplicate SKUs are
[?2004l[?2004h> collapsed to the highest `feed_seq` (latest inserted row breaks ties), and a
[?2004l[?2004h> unique SKU index prevents new duplicates. Merchandising overrides are preserved;
[?2004l[?2004h> supplier notices are displayed for operator review, not executed as database
[?2004l[?2004h> maintenance instructions.
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
